In article <cZRfps_00WB84wW0Zi@andrew.cmu.edu> dh07+@andrew.cmu.edu (David Hairston) writes:
>problem: polymorph spells operating on "stashes" are too convenient!!!
>
>solution: give each affected item a slight chance of disintegrating.

I'm not sure about the suggested implementations but I like this idea.  It
fits in with the idea that a player can be killed by system shock when
polymorphing.  Why can't an object be destroyed because the molecular bonds
between the items were just too weak or had been weakened by several attempts
at polymorphing the object?  Different types of wands must contain different
types of magic so some form of atomic adjustment (adjustment of atoms) must
occur when a wand changes from one type to another.  This should also be true
of any other type of items.  Weapons and armor could experience system shock
for the same reason that players do.  Change a black hat into crystal plate
mail could be quit stressful.

I also suggest that cursed items always be destroyed when they are
polymorphed.  Being cursed might naturally weaken an object.

Just my opinions.                                               Marc
